# Gateway for the OpenVibe LLM inference worker.
#
# llama.cpp listens only on loopback; this is the only public listener. It adds the two endpoints
# llama.cpp does not have as separate paths:
#
#   GET /ready    the same check as llama.cpp GET /health, so a slot/model that is not loaded is
#                 not ready. The orchestrator removes the worker from rotation when this is not 2xx.
#   GET /health   passed through to llama.cpp.
#   GET /metrics  passed through, Prometheus text.
#
# Everything else (OpenAI-compatible chat/completions, props, slots, ...) is passed through
# unchanged. Streaming responses are flushed immediately. Dynamic LoRA management is not exposed:
# the worker starts no LoRA and the vLLM-style load/unload paths are refused here as well.
#
# DRAIN_SECONDS is also the gateway's shutdown grace period: on SIGTERM Caddy stops accepting new
# connections and waits up to this long for in-flight requests before the entrypoint stops
# llama.cpp.

{
	admin off
	auto_https off
	persist_config off
	grace_period {$DRAIN_SECONDS}s
}

:{$PORT} {
	@lora path /lora* /v1/load_lora_adapter* /v1/unload_lora_adapter*
	respond @lora 404

	@ready path /ready
	handle @ready {
		rewrite * /health
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$LLM_PORT} {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$LLM_PORT} {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}
}
